 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the real property tax law, in relation to the certification of\nfinal state equalization rates",
    "basePrintNo": "S6958",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6958-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1212, RPT L",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Tax Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6958\n\nSPONSOR: AMEDORE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the real property tax law, in relation\nto the certification of final state equalization rates\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nSets a statutory deadline for certification of equalization rates.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Section 1212 of the real property tax law, as amended by\nchapter 355 of the laws of 1990 and as further amended by subdivision\n(b) of section 1 of part W of chapter 56 of the laws of 2010.\n\nSection 2: Effective Date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIn cases when a municipality appeals an equalization rate determined by\nthe New York State Office of Real Property Tax Services, there is\ncurrently no statutory deadline by which appeals must be finalized,\nmeaning that in some cases the final determination of the total property\ntax bill for a given homeowner may not be finalized until mere weeks\nbefore the issuance of property tax bills.  This bill requires that\nthese appeals are finalized a minimum of thirty days before these bills\nare issued- allowing taxpayers to better anticipate the financial impact\nof their property tax bill.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone to state\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
